<title>USA: Amgen files patent suit.</title>
<headline>Amgen files patent suit.</headline>
<dateline>THOUSAND OAKS, Calif. 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Amgen Inc on Wednesday said it has filed a patent infringement lawsuit in federal court against Transkaryotic Therapies Inc and Hoechst AG unit, Hoechst Marion Roussel.</p>
<p>The suit alleges infringement of several U.S. patents owned by Amgen centering on an erythropoietin product and processes for making erythropoietin (EPO). The suit asks for an injunction barring the defendants from making, importing, using or selling EPO in the United States, Amgen said in a statement.  </p>
<p>Amgen also said the U.S. Patent and Trademark Office had issued to it a patent for additional product claims for EPO, providing further protection against unauthorized making, importation, use or sale of EPO in the United States.</p>
